  "title": "Kuwait Towers",
  "summary": "Kuwait Towers are three slender towers on a small peninsula in northern Kuwait City, designed by Malene Bjørn for the Swedish firm VBB as part of a national water-supply network. Two towers store 9000 cubic metres of water; the third holds floodlights. They became a symbol of national identity.",
